The error you are encountering is due to an attempt to mutate the Redux state directly. The state in Redux should be treated as immutable; you should always return a new state object instead of modifying the existing one.

The issue seems to be originating from the `handleNodeTap` function in the `VisNetwork.js` component. When you call `fetchData(nodeId)`, it is attempting to mutate the state between dispatches.

To fix the issue, you should update the `handleNodeTap` function to dispatch an action instead of calling `fetchData` directly. Update the function as follows:
```javascript
const handleNodeTap = async (event) => {
  if (!cyInstance) return;

  var nodeData = event.target.data();
  var nodeId = '';
  console.log('Tapped node data:', nodeData);
  if (!nodeData.data) {
    nodeId = nodeData.id;
  } else {
    nodeId = nodeData.data.id;
  }
  console.log('Tapped node id:', nodeId);

  // Dispatch fetchData action instead of calling it directly
  await dispatch(fetchData(nodeId));
};
```
By making this change, you ensure that Redux handles the state update correctly without any direct mutation of the state. This should resolve the error you are encountering.

